        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#ffffff;font-family:Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:3px solid #0f172a;border-bottom:1px solid #0f172a;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>TUTORIAL · interface</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:500 clamp(40px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;text-wrap:balance;color:#0f172a'>Getting around</h1><p style='margin:18px 0 0;max-width:36ch;font:italic 400 clamp(20px,3.6cqw,26px)/1.35 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#475569'>One rule: a click on a thing brings you one step closer to it.</p></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;flex-direction:row-reverse;align-items:flex-start;gap:32px 40px'><div style='flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0'><section data-role='settings' style='padding-top:10px;border-top:3px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0f172a'>At a glance</h2><dl style='margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;column-gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1'><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Encoded as</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>an authored graph consumed as an edge-class resource; distinct from an Edge instance</dd></dl></section></div><div style='flex:999 1 380px;min-width:0'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>The rule</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><span style='float:left;padding:6px 10px 0 0;font:500 68px/54px Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'>E</span>verything is seen at some distance. A click on a thing brings you one step closer to it, and stepping out takes you one step back. For a node there are three steps. If it is far or small, the camera comes to it. If it is in view, it takes focus at a size you can read. If it already has focus, you are inside it: its text scrolls and its links answer. A double-click goes straight to the last step.</p></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Try it</h2><ol style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:26px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>While browsing, click a node that is far away. The camera comes to it.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Click it again. It takes focus and is brought to reading size.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Click it a third time. You are inside it and can scroll and follow its links.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Press Escape to step out of the node, and again to return to the graph as a whole.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>With a node in focus, press the right arrow to walk along the edge leaving it, and the left arrow to walk back. Where there is more than one way on, the up and down arrows choose among the edges by name.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Click an edge: the first click frames both of its ends, the second selects it, and the third travels to the end you are not at.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Press Back in the browser bar. You are returned to exactly where you were.</li></ol></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>What to know</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>A drag moves, and a click travels: dragging never takes you anywhere. It moves the node, or pans the view when the node is pinned or you drag empty space. A click never moves anything. A Portal takes the same steps as a node, and its last step goes through to the graph it opens; an Enter button on it does the same in one press. A link inside a page takes one click, because you are already inside. While you are editing, a click selects a node and does not travel, so you never leave the graph you are working on by surprise.</p></section></div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": ""
      }
    },
